    -## The one place the trap reappears
    +at every commit. Concretely: your code stages a `DepositMoneyAction`; the executor opens the
    +transaction, writes the `wallets` row, writes the matching `MoneyDepositedEvent` to `events`, and
    +commits. **There is no second table to remember, because you never write to it.**
    +That is the whole pitch, and the rest of this section is how the pieces make the guarantee
    +*structural* rather than a convention somebody has to police. An action that forgot the outbox
    +is not a bug you can write - there is no API for writing a domain row without one.
    +## The one place it reappears
    -[Sharding](sharding.md) and [Sagas](sagas.md).
    +[sharding strategies](/learn/sharding-strategies/) and [sagas](/learn/sagas/).
    +<LearnPager current="the-dual-write-trap" />
    -- [The outbox](outbox.md) - the table and the write path
    -- [Actions](actions.md) - the two-phase lifecycle that makes it automatic
    -- [Sagas](sagas.md) - coordinating multi-step work without pretending it is one transaction
