    -# The transaction manager
    -The executor is the right entry point for **business operations** - anything that changes a
    -domain object and emits events. Sometimes you need transactional access outside that: an admin
    -script backfilling a column, a startup hook reconciling two tables, a multi-step read that does
    -not fit the action shape, batch maintenance with no event worth emitting.
    -`fetch(mapper)` family a repository uses, described in [Repositories](repositories.md#examples).
    +`fetch(mapper)` family a repository uses, described in [Repositories](/reference/repository/#turning-rows-into-objects).
    +**A failed commit is not on its own grounds for eviction.** The `COMMIT` is issued inside the
    +`try`, so a commit that raises falls into the same `except` as any other failure and gets a
    +`ROLLBACK` like any other transaction. If that rollback succeeds, the connection is clean and
    +goes back to the pool normally. Only a rollback that *also* fails leaves the state unknown, and
    +only then is the connection thrown away.
    -`tx_db_else_db`. See [Repositories](../database/repositories.md).
    +`tx_db_else_db`. See [Repositories](/reference/repository/).
    -  [Concurrency](../runtime/concurrency.md).
    +  [Concurrency](/reference/runtime/concurrency/).
    -connections deliberately - see [Repositories](../database/repositories.md#picking-the-right-one).
    +connections deliberately - see [Repositories](/reference/repository/#picking-the-right-one).
    -partial commit would need compensating, use a [saga](../concepts/sagas.md).
    +partial commit would need compensating, use a [saga](/learn/sagas/).
    -- [Actions](../concepts/actions.md) - the recommended path, which uses this internally
    -- [Repositories](repositories.md) - what joins the open transaction, and what does not
    -- [Sharding](sharding.md) - one manager per shard
